<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70056" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νει-όθεν</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		Adv. (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέατος</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from the bottom,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεστενάχιζε ν. ἐκ κραδίης</span> he
			heaved a sigh <i>from the bottom</i> of his heart, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ἐλάτην] ν. ἔλλαβε χερσίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1197
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				234
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἐξεμέσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cerc.
					4.55
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[βλ?]ύσε ν.</span> Epic.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				7.10
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νειόθε</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. δ᾽ ἐξανέηκεν . . πηγήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					4.467.25
				</span></i>
			 (Didyma, <span class="entity">iii A.D.</span>); in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. δρᾶν</span>”
				<i>heartily,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Peregr.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. Cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεόθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
